Offer the system folder picker from File > Open Folder on Android.

Open Folder in the web workbench is the quick input that asks for a path. On a phone that
dialog starts in the app's own storage and lists what the app itself can read. A folder in
shared storage (Documents, Download, an SD card) is empty there, because Android hides what
other apps saved from a path and only the system picker grants access to it. The picker is
the saf-bridge command vscodroid.openFolderFromDevice, but only the command palette, the
remote indicator menu and the empty Explorer reached it. The File menu, Ctrl+K Ctrl+O, the
palette's own Open Folder and the Explorer's Open Folder button all end in pickFolderAndOpen,
and each of them showed the typed dialog.

pickFolderAndOpen now runs the picker straight away when the page runs on Android and the
command is registered: no question, and no way into the typed dialog. The app keeps the user's
work on public storage (/storage/emulated/0/.VScoderoid-Pro) and opens any other folder through
the system picker, so a dialog that browses the app's private storage has nothing to offer. Open
in a new window keeps the typed dialog, because the picker opens its folder in the current
window. Add Folder to Workspace, Save As and Open File do not go through this function and are
untouched.

The command is registered once the bundled extension has activated, which is a few seconds
after a page loads. Until then, and when the extension is missing, the typed dialog shows
alone, as it did before. That check is load-bearing: executeCommand on an id that nothing
registered waits up to 30 seconds for an activation event before it rejects. A command that
fails falls back to the typed dialog and logs a warning.

